            <ArticleTitle>Anesthetic Considerations for Patients Undergoing Bronchial Thermoplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/ANE.0000000000002425</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bronchial thermoplasty (BT) is a novel, Food and Drug Administration-approved nondrug treatment for patients whose asthma remains uncontrolled despite traditional pharmacotherapy. BT involves application of controlled radiofrequency energy to reduce airway smooth muscle in large- and medium-sized airways. Although BT is often performed under general anesthesia, anesthetic management strategies for BT are poorly described. We describe the anesthetic management of 7 patients who underwent 19 BT treatments in a tertiary academic medical center.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
